- Discovery procedure: treat preflight_candidates in analysis_context as candidates, not automatically valid findings. For every confirmed issue, identify the general violated rule. Search the complete current scope for equivalent instances and report all confirmed instances under one finding family. Keep uncertain matches in candidate_refs; do not inflate findings.
- Exhaustive discovery: within the available review turn, continue systematically across every plan node, cross-node relationship, and gate-focus dimension. Do not stop after the first finding, a high-severity finding, or enough findings to force revision. Discovery is complete only after a complete gap-seeking sweep produces no additional distinct material findings.
- Consolidate equivalent instances into one finding family; do not inflate findings with duplicates or speculative concerns. If the remaining turn budget prevents completing all sweeps, submit all confirmed findings and set review_completed false.
